/**
 * @file README.dox
 * @brief Overview of the built-in disambiguation library.
 *
 * @ingroup disambstd_api
 *
 * The `disambstd` directory contains the standard ambiguity-resolution
 * strategies that can be attached to a `glr_parser_t` through
 * `glr_parser_add_disambiguator()`.
 *
 * All twenty strategies share the named/enum factory and options in
 * `include/glr/disambstd.h`. Runtime families include operator selection,
 * predicates, semantics, memoized costs, probability, attributes, lexical
 * restrictions, layout, island coverage, name resolution, and post-parse
 * filtering. SAT/SMT bounded analysis and counterexample-guided refinement
 * also expose a standalone grammar-analysis API with witness reports.
 *
 * See `disambstd/README.md` for callback contracts, bounds, examples, and
 * downstream CMake integration. Legacy factories in
 * `include/glr/disambiguate.h` remain supported.
 */
